# 7. Integrate the Existing Vertical Slice Mechanics

The unique Chrono Rig gameplay must remain central to the campaign.

Do not reduce the game to ordinary melee combat with dialogue between encounters.

Use the existing systems meaningfully:

### Chrono Rig Recording
Use recorded player actions to solve environmental problems and reveal narrative information.

### Independent Echo Playback
Echoes should remain independent of the live player and should not create recursive recordings or duplicate rewards.

### Phase Relay
Use Relay for tactical encounters and appropriate environmental traversal.

### Resonance and Convergence
Make synchronized Echo/player combat meaningful against appropriate enemies and bosses.

### Skill Tree
Make Duelist, Conductor, and Wayfinder paths meaningful.

Each path should offer different gameplay expression while remaining reasonably balanced.

### Bosses
Connect each major boss's mechanics and narrative role to its chapter.

HELIX-04 must retain its existing three-phase encounter unless inspection finds a demonstrable defect.

Build out the Choir, Curator, Matron, and final Chronicle Loom encounters using the established boss architecture where available.

Do not blindly copy HELIX-04's mechanics to every boss.

